Inside the grid container you define the number and size of the grid columns 
and rows.

For this, we will use the following properties:

Thegrid-template-columnsproperty 
defines the number and width of the columns in the grid.

The value is a space-separated-list, where each value defines the width 
of the respective column.

Common values are:

To create a grid layout with 3 columns of equal width, use the "auto" 
keyword.

To create a grid layout with 3 columns: 2 columns with a fixed width, and 
1 column with size "auto".

Thefrunit stands for "fraction". 
This unit automatically divides the available space into fractions.

1fr will take 1 fraction of the available space, while 2fr will take 
2 fractions of the available space.

The CSSrepeat()function is used to repeat a set of columns or rows in a grid.

The CSSminmax()function is used to 
define a size-range greater than or equal to a min value and less than or equal to a max value.

Thegrid-template-rowsproperty 
defines the number and height of the rows in the grid.

The value is a space-separated-list, where each value defines the height of the respective row.

Common values are:

### Code Snippets

```
.container {
display: grid;
grid-template-columns: auto auto auto;
}

---

.container {
display: grid;
grid-template-columns: 80px 200px auto;
}

---

.container {
display: grid;
grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr;
}

---

.container {
display: grid;
grid-template-columns: 1fr 2fr 1fr;
}

---

.container {
display: grid;
grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
}

---

.container {
display: grid;
grid-template-columns: minmax(80px, 1fr) 150px 150px;
}

---

.container {
display: grid;
grid-template-rows: 80px 200px;
}
```
